+## THE THIRD VOICE -- ALIVE, UNDEGRADED, AND REACHING NOBODY  (issue 0675).
+##
+## THE STATE NEITHER EXISTING SENTENCE CAN DESCRIBE, and it is the user's own:
+## the CIW toplevel mapped with its text pane destroyed. Not DEGRADED (the live
+## `::xschem::notify` is the full four-sink channel), not a FAULT (nothing
+## raised) -- so at HEAD the channel returned 1, the witness named a sink, and
+## the log carried no word of any kind about a notice that reached no human.
+## 0497 rule 2 is split by CAUSE, never one aggregate: a third cause gets a
+## third sentence, not a re-wording of one of the other two.
+##
+## ⚠ THE MARKER CONTAINS NEITHER GOLDEN SUBSTRING. `NOTICE CHANNEL DEGRADED`
+## and `NOTICE CHANNEL FAULT` are grepped literally by NTD1/4/6/9/11/12,
+## PS20/23/27/29/32/33 and SG14/SG18, and their ABSENCE is asserted by several
+## of them. `UNREACHABLE` is a third word on purpose.
+##
+## THREE TERMS, AND EACH ONE EXCLUDES A WRONG FIX:
+##   * NOT the bootstrap -- the DEGRADED sentence already owns that state and
+##     already says where notices go;
+##   * Tk IS live -- a `--nogui` session has no visible sink by construction,
+##     and announcing there would add a line to every headless batch run and a
+##     SECOND `#! ` line to the degraded child SG14 counts (0497 rule 1);
+##   * no arm is `visible` -- `blind` still counts as unreachable (a withdrawn
+##     pane RECEIVES the text and no eye is on it), which is the distinction
